// A binding may not reuse the name of a top-level function declared in its OWN file (E0059) — even
// though every declaration in a package carries a derived, dotted module path. Inferring "merged in
// from another module" from the dot silently turned this check off for all packaged code: the
// binding was swallowed, `count` kept meaning the function, and nothing said so.
//
// The sibling `desk.tools.total` is not reported: it is another module's name, and this file never
// imports it.
// expect: error E0059 at 14:1
// expect: exit 1
fn count(): int {
    return 99
}

count = 5;
echo count;
